WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.164 --> 00:00:02.296
(cheerful music)

00:00:02.296 --> 00:00:03.941
- So I was just in Los Angeles.

00:00:03.941 --> 00:00:04.774
- Hi Steven.

00:00:04.774 --> 00:00:05.840
- Hanging out with you guys.

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:08.404
Now we're all in New York City, Big Apple.

00:00:08.404 --> 00:00:10.036
And today we are doing curry!

00:00:10.036 --> 00:00:11.777
Right now we are at a
Malaysian coffee shop.

00:00:11.777 --> 00:00:13.261
This place is called Kopitiam.

00:00:13.261 --> 00:00:15.601
And curry is a very personal thing to me.

00:00:15.601 --> 00:00:18.225
Some of the locations in
this episode were biased

00:00:18.225 --> 00:00:21.324
by my personal
Chinese-Malaysian background.

00:00:21.324 --> 00:00:23.873
Hence the coffee shop we're at right now.

00:00:23.873 --> 00:00:24.706
Woo yes.

00:00:24.953 --> 00:00:25.786
Whoa!

00:00:25.786 --> 00:00:26.777
- [Andrew] Certified awesome.

00:00:26.777 --> 00:00:27.950
- [Steven] This is literally

00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:30.050
how stuff is served in Malaysia.

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:32.614
My favorite dish in the
world probably is Roti Canai,

00:00:32.614 --> 00:00:36.019
which is a Malaysian
dish influenced by India.

00:00:36.019 --> 00:00:37.121
- [Andrew] Are we gonna try that today?

00:00:37.121 --> 00:00:38.741
- They do have it at one of the places

00:00:38.741 --> 00:00:39.975
that we're eating at.

00:00:39.975 --> 00:00:40.808
- We should eat it!

00:00:40.808 --> 00:00:41.641
- Okay!

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:42.474
- It's your favorite food.

00:00:42.474 --> 00:00:44.147
- Today we're gonna be
trying three curry dishes

00:00:44.147 --> 00:00:45.678
at three drastically
different price points

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:48.946
to find out which curry is the
most worth it at its price.

00:00:48.946 --> 00:00:50.096
I'm gonna hit you

00:00:50.096 --> 00:00:51.009
with a curry fact!

00:00:51.009 --> 00:00:53.472
17th century British
colonizers were perplexed

00:00:53.472 --> 00:00:55.214
by the variety of dishes in India

00:00:55.214 --> 00:00:57.053
and categorized them all
under the term "curry".

00:00:57.053 --> 00:00:58.546
People who visited India,

00:00:58.546 --> 00:00:59.751
they didn't know how to categorize

00:00:59.751 --> 00:01:01.032
all of these different foods.

00:01:01.032 --> 00:01:03.633
So instead of actually identifying
and learning all of them,

00:01:03.633 --> 00:01:06.185
they just lumped them into one category.

00:01:06.185 --> 00:01:07.899
- Before curry, you would just call it

00:01:07.899 --> 00:01:09.584
what the individual dish name was.

00:01:09.584 --> 00:01:10.417
- Exactly.

00:01:10.417 --> 00:01:12.208
Okay so the first place
we're going to is a bakery.

00:01:12.208 --> 00:01:13.895
And we'll be having some curry puffs.

00:01:13.895 --> 00:01:15.035
- Curry puffs.

00:01:15.035 --> 00:01:16.837
So like a little pastry of curry, huh?

00:01:16.837 --> 00:01:19.490
I got my drink to go, how about you?

00:01:19.490 --> 00:01:20.665
- I might get one of those bags.

00:01:20.665 --> 00:01:22.769
(energetic beats)

00:01:22.769 --> 00:01:24.062
- Hi, my name is James Chou.

00:01:24.062 --> 00:01:25.306
This is my father Han chou.

00:01:25.306 --> 00:01:26.398
We're at Fay Da Bakery,

00:01:26.398 --> 00:01:29.396
and we will be showing
you our curry beef puff.

00:01:29.396 --> 00:01:33.479
- [Han Chou] (speaks in Chinese)

00:01:53.222 --> 00:01:54.653
- [James Chou] So basically
the dough is mixed

00:01:54.653 --> 00:01:55.963
same process as croissant.

00:01:55.963 --> 00:01:58.779
So in there we use shortening
and margarine to fold it in,

00:01:58.779 --> 00:02:00.304
goes through that automated sheeter,

00:02:00.304 --> 00:02:01.212
a little egg wash,

00:02:01.212 --> 00:02:03.919
and then we have everyone putting
the filling into each one,

00:02:03.919 --> 00:02:05.561
baked and then you take it out

00:02:05.561 --> 00:02:07.029
after about 20, 25 minutes,

00:02:07.029 --> 00:02:07.990
you do egg wash,

00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:10.256
and then you put it back in
for another 15, 20 minutes,

00:02:10.256 --> 00:02:11.756
and then you do one final egg wash.

00:02:11.756 --> 00:02:13.608
- [Steven] What makes
a very good curry puff?

00:02:13.608 --> 00:02:17.691
- [Han Chou] (speaks in Chinese)

00:02:23.914 --> 00:02:24.747
(register bell sound)

00:02:24.747 --> 00:02:27.241
- [Steven] I got a watermelon
smoothie to start off our day.

00:02:27.241 --> 00:02:28.348
We'll be eating a lot of curries.

00:02:28.348 --> 00:02:29.494
I gotta balance it out.

00:02:29.494 --> 00:02:31.798
- I'm having ice malted milk drink.

00:02:31.798 --> 00:02:32.631
- What?

00:02:32.631 --> 00:02:33.464
- Yeah it's called Horlicks.

00:02:33.464 --> 00:02:34.947
- Wow I didn't even know this existed.

00:02:34.947 --> 00:02:35.780
Cheers!

00:02:37.712 --> 00:02:38.545
- Here's one for you.

00:02:38.545 --> 00:02:39.378
- Yes!

00:02:39.378 --> 00:02:41.210
The most familiar smell

00:02:41.210 --> 00:02:42.289
in the world to me.

00:02:42.289 --> 00:02:43.426
Chinese bakery smell,

00:02:43.426 --> 00:02:45.772
that was the Sunday afternoon,

00:02:45.772 --> 00:02:47.149
family goes out to lunch,

00:02:47.149 --> 00:02:48.681
and we hit a bakery afterwards.

00:02:48.681 --> 00:02:49.514
Cheers.

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:52.931
- It's extremely satisfying,

00:02:52.931 --> 00:02:55.759
because you have a very
buttery nice pastry

00:02:55.759 --> 00:02:58.147
along with a very savory filling.

00:02:58.147 --> 00:02:59.270
It's not spicy.

00:02:59.270 --> 00:03:00.900
It is actually a little sweet.

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:02.012
- It's like a pie.

00:03:02.012 --> 00:03:02.932
It's like a ham pie.

00:03:02.932 --> 00:03:03.765
- Yeah.

00:03:03.765 --> 00:03:04.598
I think it's really cool

00:03:04.598 --> 00:03:07.161
that you can have this savory treat

00:03:07.161 --> 00:03:10.578
at what is predominantly a sweets bakery.

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:12.257
The fact that you can come to this bakery

00:03:12.257 --> 00:03:13.850
and you can really build out

00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:15.652
like a pretty well-balanced meal,

00:03:15.652 --> 00:03:17.866
that's pretty unique I think, you know?

00:03:17.866 --> 00:03:20.616
- I think it's a beautiful thing.

00:03:21.032 --> 00:03:22.746
- [Andrew] Adam why are you
eating that like a squirrel?

00:03:22.746 --> 00:03:24.557
- [Annie] (laughs)

00:03:24.557 --> 00:03:26.222
- So we just ate a curry puff,

00:03:26.222 --> 00:03:28.416
but we're going to a
Malaysian restaurant next.

00:03:28.416 --> 00:03:30.424
So to prepare our appetite,

00:03:30.424 --> 00:03:33.924
I was thinking that we bust open a durian,

00:03:33.956 --> 00:03:36.098
which is the king of fruits in Malaysia.

00:03:36.098 --> 00:03:37.462
Durian is a fruit that I've seen people,

00:03:37.462 --> 00:03:41.336
kind of, laugh at, the
smelliest fruit in the world,

00:03:41.336 --> 00:03:43.559
but honestly, durian is a fruit

00:03:43.559 --> 00:03:46.523
that my family, the first thing that we do

00:03:46.523 --> 00:03:49.287
when we land in Malaysia
when we visit is eat durian.

00:03:49.287 --> 00:03:50.120
- Really?

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:50.953
- Yeah.

00:03:50.953 --> 00:03:51.998
You just cut open a little bit

00:03:51.998 --> 00:03:53.191
(durian cracks)

00:03:53.191 --> 00:03:54.024
Oh!

00:03:55.506 --> 00:03:57.071
- It doesn't smell that bad,

00:03:57.071 --> 00:03:58.743
it smells like cheese honestly.

00:03:58.743 --> 00:03:59.576
- Cheers.

00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:05.357
- Oh it tastes good!

00:04:05.631 --> 00:04:06.464
- Yeah.

00:04:06.464 --> 00:04:08.749
- It's like a cross between a banana,

00:04:08.749 --> 00:04:10.832
a pineapple, and a mango.

00:04:10.944 --> 00:04:12.113
Hit me with that curry fact.

00:04:12.113 --> 00:04:13.097
- Curry fact!

00:04:13.097 --> 00:04:16.388
People who enjoy action
movies and adventure seekers

00:04:16.388 --> 00:04:19.402
are six times more likely
to like spicy food.

00:04:19.402 --> 00:04:20.704
- I love action movies.

00:04:20.704 --> 00:04:21.680
I like spicy food.

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:24.347
I like getting my face to sweat.

00:04:24.498 --> 00:04:25.331
- I've seen you sweat.

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:27.364
The next place we're going to is Laut.

00:04:27.364 --> 00:04:28.303
It's Malaysian food.

00:04:28.303 --> 00:04:31.712
- So you like this next
place a little, or a "Laut"?

00:04:31.712 --> 00:04:33.962
- (laughs)

00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:34.943
A "Laut".

00:04:35.001 --> 00:04:37.834
(energetic music)

00:04:38.181 --> 00:04:39.425
- My name is Salil Mehta.

00:04:39.425 --> 00:04:41.265
We're at Laut in Union Square.

00:04:41.265 --> 00:04:43.701
And we're gonna be having the
best Curry Laksa in the world.

00:04:43.701 --> 00:04:44.534
- Oh wow.

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:45.533
- Wow.

00:04:45.533 --> 00:04:47.054
- [Salil Mehta] Seven years
ago, people did not know

00:04:47.054 --> 00:04:49.280
much about a Rendang, much about a Laksa,

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:51.358
but a lot of people opened those doors up,

00:04:51.358 --> 00:04:53.308
and then my background
is slightly different

00:04:53.308 --> 00:04:55.077
from most of the Malaysian restaurants

00:04:55.077 --> 00:04:56.021
that are in New York City.

00:04:56.021 --> 00:04:58.821
Being Indian, I was bringing
the Indian influence behind.

00:04:58.821 --> 00:05:00.093
- [Steven] So today we're
having the Curry Laksa.

00:05:00.093 --> 00:05:00.926
- Yes.

00:05:00.926 --> 00:05:02.491
- Which is exactly what
you're talking about,

00:05:02.491 --> 00:05:04.893
the Chinese influence with the
Malayan and Indian influence.

00:05:04.893 --> 00:05:07.003
- Laksa comes from
(speaks foreign phrase),

00:05:07.003 --> 00:05:08.248
which means one million flavors.

00:05:08.248 --> 00:05:10.027
You have all these great, amazing,

00:05:10.027 --> 00:05:12.410
different kinds of Laksas
all over Southeast Asia.

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:14.471
Then you have interaction
of different cultures.

00:05:14.471 --> 00:05:15.968
You have the Indian marrying the Malay,

00:05:15.968 --> 00:05:17.090
the Malay marrying the Chinese.

00:05:17.090 --> 00:05:18.939
Our Laksa, this is more,

00:05:18.939 --> 00:05:20.683
Malay-Indian influenced Curry Laksa.

00:05:20.683 --> 00:05:21.617
So the way we do ours,

00:05:21.617 --> 00:05:24.634
we use onion, ginger,
barley, fresh lemongrass,

00:05:24.634 --> 00:05:26.305
grind it all up together in a paste,

00:05:26.305 --> 00:05:28.486
cook it low and slow with some fresh curry

00:05:28.486 --> 00:05:29.880
leaves brown spices in it.

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:31.360
Add the coconut milk slowly,

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:32.568
and we do a Lai Fun noodle.

00:05:32.568 --> 00:05:34.154
This is like tapioca starch noodle.

00:05:34.154 --> 00:05:35.597
And we do egg round noodle,

00:05:35.597 --> 00:05:36.996
which is like a Lo Mein noodle.

00:05:36.996 --> 00:05:38.756
Take some tofu puff actually soaks

00:05:38.756 --> 00:05:40.383
in the soup from the Laksa.

00:05:40.383 --> 00:05:43.332
I believe that Curry Laksa
with seafood goes best.

00:05:43.332 --> 00:05:44.455
Put the soup together,

00:05:44.455 --> 00:05:46.377
garnish with some cucumber, lime.

00:05:46.377 --> 00:05:47.807
That your bowl of Laksa.

00:05:47.807 --> 00:05:48.906
- So we weren't planning on coming here

00:05:48.906 --> 00:05:49.976
to eat the Roti Canai.

00:05:49.976 --> 00:05:51.123
But saw in the menu,

00:05:51.123 --> 00:05:53.667
so, could we also do that virtual quick?

00:05:53.667 --> 00:05:55.649
- Roti's most popular
dish in the restaurant.

00:05:55.649 --> 00:05:57.182
Roti's something really unique and amazing

00:05:57.182 --> 00:05:58.991
because it can be had as a snack,

00:05:58.991 --> 00:06:00.767
it can be had as a proper meal as well.

00:06:00.767 --> 00:06:02.838
The dough is prepped in pure Desi ghee.

00:06:02.838 --> 00:06:05.094
So that's the way it
was traditionally made

00:06:05.094 --> 00:06:06.272
by bom in Malaysia.

00:06:06.272 --> 00:06:08.153
And it comes from Canai, India,

00:06:08.153 --> 00:06:10.173
so that's where the Canai come from.

00:06:10.173 --> 00:06:12.137
- He just asked me if we wanna share this.

00:06:12.137 --> 00:06:12.970
No!

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:13.803
There's a rule.

00:06:13.803 --> 00:06:14.636
- Okay Steven.

00:06:14.636 --> 00:06:15.886
- Two people, two roti.

00:06:15.886 --> 00:06:17.652
This is actually my favorite dish,

00:06:17.652 --> 00:06:20.603
because it reminds me
of my time in Malaysia

00:06:20.603 --> 00:06:21.787
staying with my grandpa.

00:06:21.787 --> 00:06:24.138
And we would walk down to the local cart,

00:06:24.138 --> 00:06:25.571
and they would just fry this up,

00:06:25.571 --> 00:06:27.111
and hand me the curry in a bag.

00:06:27.111 --> 00:06:28.005
I wouldn't even wait till I got home,

00:06:28.005 --> 00:06:29.061
I would just eat on the way home

00:06:29.061 --> 00:06:29.970
- That sounds awesome.

00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:30.803
Cheers.

00:06:30.847 --> 00:06:33.514
(tongue clicks)

00:06:35.747 --> 00:06:37.197
Oh man that's good.

00:06:37.197 --> 00:06:38.198
- Perfectly crispy.

00:06:38.198 --> 00:06:39.772
It's almost like a croissant.

00:06:39.772 --> 00:06:40.945
How flaky this one is.

00:06:40.945 --> 00:06:42.919
- You have like the best textured bread,

00:06:42.919 --> 00:06:46.330
and you get to just put it
in the most luxurious gravy.

00:06:46.330 --> 00:06:47.673
It cannot get better than that.

00:06:47.673 --> 00:06:48.840
- Gravy makes everything good.

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:51.507
And now we have the Curry Laksa.

00:06:51.801 --> 00:06:53.457
- So this is so pretty.

00:06:53.457 --> 00:06:55.087
I love the color of the broth

00:06:55.087 --> 00:06:57.499
that it's speckled with the oil.

00:06:57.499 --> 00:07:00.947
- It's the million flavors
of spice and color.

00:07:00.947 --> 00:07:02.555
- Gotta make sure you
don't lose any noodles.

00:07:02.555 --> 00:07:04.400
- And then you know get some seafood.

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:06.650
The tofu is a flavor saver.

00:07:06.826 --> 00:07:09.338
This is the mustache of ingredients.

00:07:09.338 --> 00:07:11.703
This is what soaks the curry up.

00:07:11.703 --> 00:07:12.884
And then you just take a little bite.

00:07:12.884 --> 00:07:13.732
- I love that.

00:07:13.732 --> 00:07:15.217
The mustache of ingredients.

00:07:15.217 --> 00:07:16.652
What are you gonna try first, noodle?

00:07:16.652 --> 00:07:18.420
Or just broth on its own?

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:19.893
- Uh let's do broth.

00:07:19.893 --> 00:07:21.976
(slurps)

00:07:22.798 --> 00:07:24.906
- It changes in your
mouth as you're eating it.

00:07:24.906 --> 00:07:26.922
- I like this too, because
you have the coconut

00:07:26.922 --> 00:07:29.008
and the curry just living together

00:07:29.008 --> 00:07:32.892
but also porting their own
identity and color here.

00:07:32.892 --> 00:07:34.975
(slurps)

00:07:38.141 --> 00:07:39.594
- I understand how this is like

00:07:39.594 --> 00:07:41.760
a dish that emerged as the marriage

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:43.918
from a lot of people and the cuisines,

00:07:43.918 --> 00:07:46.958
because it is like so
many all-star things.

00:07:46.958 --> 00:07:48.331
You have noodles, you have seafood,

00:07:48.331 --> 00:07:49.877
you have this amazing broth.

00:07:49.877 --> 00:07:51.138
- I save the flavors here for the end.

00:07:51.138 --> 00:07:53.074
It's been just in here
collecting juice, by the way.

00:07:53.074 --> 00:07:53.907
My sponge.

00:07:54.172 --> 00:07:55.005
Cheers.

00:07:55.005 --> 00:07:55.838
- Cheers.

00:07:57.980 --> 00:07:59.856
- (coughs)

00:07:59.856 --> 00:08:00.689
Curry!

00:08:01.343 --> 00:08:02.176
I love it.

00:08:02.176 --> 00:08:04.427
Alright, so we just had some great Laksa.

